131-At the agents level the breadcrumb `Sessions › <project> › <short ID>` moves from the footer to the top border, right after the title: `┌─ 󰚩 Agent usage › app (Sessions › ~/w/app › 1a2b3c4d) ───┐`. The footer loses a row (4 to 3; 6 to 5 with the filter bar); the tab row stays under the table. Reason: the user asked for the trail on the frame, in parentheses, stuck to the title (they first chose the right edge, then went back on it). Mechanism: an optional `FrameTrailView` interface, the budget from `theme.BorderTrailBudget`, the line from `theme.RenderBorderTitleTrail`; a trail too wide is dropped, never cut. Alternatives rejected: concatenating into `GetTitle()` (one style, pollutes the palette and help titles, no clean degradation) and splicing with `overlay.Compose` (duplicates the column arithmetic). Accepted costs: the project name appears twice, side by side (title leaf, then end of the path); and `:jobs` keeps its breadcrumb under the table, a declared inconsistency (Rule 123 exception).
